  "assessment": "The change replaces UTF-8 byte counting with ASCII-only character counting by silently dropping all non-ASCII characters via `encode(\"ascii\", \"ignore\")`. This successfully prevents multi-byte padding attacks but fundamentally shifts the length metric from codepoints/bytes to a strict subset count. Consequently, any password composed entirely of non-ASCII characters will be reduced to an empty string and fail validation regardless of its actual visual length.",
