      "defect": "Over-rejection of valid Unicode passwords due to silent character stripping. The original rule counted UTF-8 bytes, allowing any codepoint contribution to length. The new implementation discards all non-ASCII characters entirely, meaning passwords that meet the minimum threshold by grapheme or codepoint count will now fail validation.",
      "expected": "True (passes the minimum length threshold by Unicode character count)"
    }
